nCollege of Arts & Sciences News\nMedia Relations\nNews Feed\nClose the News menu\nOutreach\nWomen in Science\nTeachers & Educators\nK-12 Students\nCommunity\nClose the Outreach menu\nCollege Home\nInterdisciplinary Programs\nWater Management & Hydrological Science\nWater Management & Hydrological Science\nApply Now\nContact an Advisor\nThe Water Management and Hydrological Science (WMHS) graduate degree program is preparing the next generation of water scientists, hydrologists, and managers through teaching and research that improves the reliability and quality of water resources for human well-being and development. WMHS is supervised by an interdisciplinary faculty from multiple departments and colleges with expertise in the bio-physical, geo-chemical, management, public health, social sciences and engineering fields.\nThe program offers two masters\u2019 degrees (thesis and non-thesis options) and a doctorate. The curriculum is designed to help students become leaders in their focal areas of water, while also making connections with colleagues in other related disciplines.\nLearn More about Water Management & Hydrological Science\nProgram Overview and Requirements\nEnvironmental Programs\nInterdisciplinary Programs\nWater Management & Hydrological Science\nTexas A&M University College of Arts\n& Sciences\nGeneral Inquiries\nContact Us\nMedia Questions\nContact Us\nAbout the College\nDirectory\nDepartments & Programs\nCertificate Programs\nEvents\nUndergraduate Programs\nGraduate Programs\nIntranet\n\u00a9\nTexas A&M University\nAccessibility\nSite Policies", "links": [["Skip To Main Content", "https://artsci.tamu.edu/interdisciplinary-programs/water-mgmt-hydrological-science.html#maincontent"], ["", "https://www.tamu.edu/"], ["Texas A&M University", "https://www.tamu.edu/"], ["College of Arts & Sciences", "https://artsci.tamu.edu/index.html"], ["Giving", "https://artsci.tamu.edu/giving/index.html"], ["Anthropology", "https://artsci.tamu.edu/anthropology/index.ht